.TH "libnvme" 9 "enum nvme_lockdown_persistence_cdw11" "October 2026" "API Manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
enum nvme_lockdown_persistence_cdw11 \- Lockdown Persistence Personality - Command Dword 11 (Set Features)
.SH SYNOPSIS
enum nvme_lockdown_persistence_cdw11 {
.br
.BI "    NVME_LOCKDOWN_PERSISTENCE_LDPE"

};
.SH Constants
.IP "NVME_LOCKDOWN_PERSISTENCE_LDPE" 12
Lockdown Persistence Enable: If set to
'1', then Lockdown Persistence is
enabled and the prohibitions of the
Lockdown command that affect all
controllers in the NVM subsystem persist
across power cycles of the NVM subsystem.
If cleared to '0', then Lockdown
Persistence is disabled.
